{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790192138,"nonce":"Yl96tofwD4ec2mF+eziATcG4tOE=","message":"Revised 2026-09-23 (Luis): `termui` does not become `tui`; the terminal renderer sits behind `view` and `flow run` (84dfbde). `webui` becomes `gui`: `git work gui [--port N] [--no-browser]` serves every flow as a page and is the HTTP renderer of the same view specs the terminal renders, so the two surfaces are two renderers of one spec and no command exists on one and not the other. `--gui` on `view` and `flow run` sends a spec to it. Map: doc/design/cli-convention.md.","files":null}]}